cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal
  synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI assistant by
  Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "reader-ergonomics-presentations"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
abstract: >-
  How to build a presentation, academic, business or casual, so that it is
  cheap to follow and to remember, and how to draw a figure or a diagram in
  any document. An extension of reader-ergonomics: the evidence particular
  to presentations and to figures.
  Use it as a reading list and a starting point, not as an authority.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/reader-ergonomics-presentations"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - presentations
  - slides
  - pitches
  - literature review
